---
title: Gochujang buttered noodles
servings: 4
tags: [korean, quick, weeknight]
cuisine: korean
time: 25 minutes
source: Gochujang Buttered Noodles by Eric Kim, The New York Times, republished by the Honolulu Star-Advertiser, https://staradvertiser.com/?p=1244308
---

Cook the @dried pasta{1%lb}(spaghetti or other long pasta) in a #large pot{}
of well-salted boiling water. Save 1 cup of the cooking water, drain, and put
the pasta back in the pot.

Meanwhile, melt 4 tbsp of the @unsalted butter{6%tbsp} in a #skillet{} over
medium-low heat. Add the @garlic{12%cloves}(finely chopped) and a good pinch
of @kosher salt{} and stir now and then ~{1-3%minutes}, until soft but not
coloured.

Stir in the @gochujang{1/4%cup}, @honey{1/4%cup} and @sherry vinegar{1/4%cup}(or rice vinegar).
Bring to a simmer over medium-high heat, stirring, and cook
~{3-4%minutes}, until noticeably thicker. Take it off the heat.

Scrape the sauce into the pasta with the last 2 tbsp of butter and stir hard
until the butter melts, loosening with splashes of the cooking water until
glossy.

Season with salt and @black pepper{}, scatter with @?scallions{}(thinly sliced, or cilantro),
and serve at once.

> Use plain gochujang paste from a tub, not a bottled gochujang sauce.
